# Technical acceptance evolution

Authorized by the maintainer on 2026-11-01 to evolve the unconditional skill guard. Full route; no change to the original 36 technical scenarios or product permissions.

- REQ-01: All five evidence states retain their meanings; historical observations remain immutable.
- AC-01 → REQ-01: UNVERIFIED remains valid; justified INCONCLUSIVE and NOT APPLICABLE are representable; both English and legacy states obey the same rules.
- REQ-02: Technical decisions require criterion-specific execution and semantic review tied to concrete consumer/oracle inputs.
- AC-02 → REQ-02: APPROVED and REJECTED accept current reviewed executions and reject absent, stale, unrelated, documentation-only, or mismatched evidence.
- REQ-03: Governance stays portable and distinguishes snapshot acceptance from live product acceptance.
- AC-03 → REQ-03: Independent export validates without application sources; archived predecessors and existing integrity checks remain effective.
- REQ-04: Migrate only observed criteria and preserve undecided criteria and affected prior observations.
- AC-04 → REQ-04: Eight observed technical criteria are reconciled individually; three partial observations remain inconclusive; the remaining 25 technical criteria remain unverified. Affected evidence is reexamined against actual inputs.
